    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a clear focus on exploiting favorable matchups against higher-xERA arms, headlined by the elite daily efficiency score of **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88). Facing Hughes, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive 14% park factor boost and a favorable 17% SP skill adjustment, making him our cornerstone play. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Kyle Tucker** (70.45) anchor the middle and lower thirds of our lineup respectively, with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** particularly well-positioned due to a projected wind-out condition that amplifies his potential for extra-base hits against Rodriguez. While **Wade Meckler** (41.81) represents our most marginal start, his inclusion is a calculated risk against Gerrit Cole, justified by our necessity to maintain efficiency across all 5x5 categories, including the high-value speed upside he provides.\n\nThe decision to start **Jackson Merrill** (61.26) over other options was finalized by his unique profile; despite facing a lefty in Lodolo, his \"Slow SP Delivery\" factor provides a rare, actionable edge in the stolen base department, which remains our highest-weighted scarcity need. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (47.31) narrowly avoided the bench, though his score was dragged down significantly by the elite status of Williams (2.97 xERA), serving as our primary warning for potential regression today. We are also monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" statuses for **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Gunnar Henderson**, **Coby Mayo**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Kyle Tucker**, and **Luis Robert Jr.**; any unforeseen lineup shifts could trigger immediate re-evaluations. Our depth remains hampered by the absences of **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jacob Wilson**, whose IL designations continue to limit our flexibility, ensuring that fringe assets like **Sam Antonacci** (67.67) remain critical, high-scoring fixtures in our current rotation.",
